*  STEP 3 witness (conform-line-lastline-crash): &LASTFILE standalone.
*  &LASTFILE names the PREVIOUS statement's file, so a leading statement is required
*  before the read -- reading it first would answer null, not the source name.
*  It answers the source path AS INVOKED, so this witness reports only the BASENAME
*  TAIL: a bare path .ref would change with the caller's cwd and could not be pinned.
        seed = 1
        f = &LASTFILE
        f ('k30_lastfile_only.sno' RPOS(0))                                     :S(ok)F(bad)
ok      OUTPUT = 'lastfile-tail=OK'                                             :(fin)
bad     OUTPUT = 'lastfile-tail=BAD'
fin
END
